  "title": "The Repair Fair’s Little Waiting Chair",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "positive public good",
  "premise": "A volunteer wants to keep a toy repair fair organized, but people holding broken paper objects crowd the workbench. They create a clear intake tray, a numbered waiting chair, and a visible READY shelf; the final reveal shows one repaired paper bird flying a thank-you tag between all three stations.",
  "hook": "Everything is waiting in the work area.",
  "visible_action": "Objects pile on bench; three station labels appear; one numbered token moves intake to chair to ready shelf; repaired paper bird flutters overhead.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Separate arrival, work, and collection so status stays visible.",
  "gate": "Repair only paper props; real electrical, medical, structural, or safety-critical repairs require appropriate expertise.",
  "evidence_class": "fictional_demonstration",
